The PREDIMED trial showed a Mediterranean diet (predominantly plant-based) reduced major cardiovascular events by 30% versus a low-fat diet in a 7,447-person RCT.
Inflammation biomarkers (CRP, IL-6) are significantly lower in people eating predominantly plant-based diets, explaining much of the cardiovascular benefit.
Blue Zones research (Buettner) found that all five populations with unusual longevity and health eat 90–95% plant-based diets — not a coincidence across five different cultures and continents.
